"\n\n\n\n\n\n## Review\n\nVisiting Bupyeong after a long time, I saw that the familiar Canmore was still around.  \nWith fond nostalgia, I went inside with my friends without hesitation.  \n\nRiding the wave of popularity for retro relics that I personally find hard to fathom, Canmore is surprisingly considered a hot spot among younger people.  \nWhen we actually went, there was a wait, and most of the patrons were young.  \nIt seemed there were more customers visiting for a fresh new experience rather than reminiscing over old memories like us.  \n\nThe nostalgic swing was still there.  \nSeeing it again after so long brought back a lot of happy feelings.  \nThe snow shaved ice and parfait were still on the menu, and just looking at the menu reminded me of the old days.  \n\nThe unlimited toast refill that was essential back then was also available when ordering one menu item per person.  \n\nIt was great to relive old memories after a long time.  \nIt's a place I'd love to visit again whenever I think of the past.  \n\n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"